title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/unidos.jpg
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Spain.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The PSOE cannot govern by itself yet. Because we do not have an electoral majority, we need the support of other parties.

- @left: Strengthen our bonds with the left-liberal [+ ar_name +] and the radical socialist PRRS.
- @center: Strengthen our bonds with the Radical Republican Party.
- @pce: Work towards an alliance with the Communist Party.
- @minors: Improve our stance with minor republican parties, national and regional included.
- @psoe_alone: The PSOE can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard

@left
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ar_relation += 6*(1 - dissent)
go-to: left_2 if ar_name == "AR"; left_3 if ar_name == "IR" and ur_formed

The [+ ar_name +] has been one of our closest allies through the course of the Republic.

@left_2
on-arrival: prrs_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); ar_relation += 1

We have improved our relations with the [+ ar_name +] and PRSS.

@left_3
on-arrival: ur_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We have improved our relations with the [+ ar_name +] and UR.

@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; prr_relation += 2 if prr_party_leader == "Martínez Barrios"
go-to: center_op if prr_in_government = 1 and psoe_in_government = 0 and chancellor != "Lerroux"; center_coalition if psoe_in_government = 1 and prr_in_government = 1; center_bruning if chancellor = "Lerroux"

@center_op
on-arrival: prr_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the Radical-led government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@center_coalition
on-arrival: prr_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@center_bruning
on-arrival: prr_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The Lerroux conservativism makes building friendly relations difficult, but not impossible.

@pce
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pce_inter_party_seen += 1
go-to: pce_1 if pce_coalition_success = 0 and pce_relation < 40; pce_2 if pce_coalition_success = 1

@pce_1
on-arrival: pce_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if pce_inter_party_seen <= 1; prietistas_dissent += 2; prr_relation -= 2; prrs_relation -= 3; ar_relation -= 3; dlr_relation -= 5;

The communists are keep their distance from our party. However, connections are made at the grassroots and local levels.

@pce_2
on-arrival: pce_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if pce_inter_party_seen <= 1; reformist_dissent += 2; prr_relation -= 3; prrs_relation -= 3; ar_relation -= 3; dlr_relation -= 5;

After the success of the coalition government with the Communists, they are much more amenable to us.

@minors
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; other_left_republicans_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); other_right_republicans_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); dlr_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); regionalists_relation += 6*(1 - dissent)

We have improved our relation with smaller republican parties in the Cortes.

@psoe_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
